Subject: [PATCH] fix(input): cancel opposing Bedrock directional keys

Native Bedrock adds each held direction before it normalizes the move
vector, so opposing keys cancel on each axis. Upstream gives Left over
Right and Up over Down precedence instead. Replace that precedence with
cancellation, and keep the independent physical flags, diagonal
normalization and input scaling.

Keep upstream's signs: Left is +X and Up is +Y. The 1.26.60.5 client
(sha256 988f6a61...2672a) decodes the flags at 0x140493140 with the
mask table at 0x14f07eb00. MoveInput bit 15 adds +1 to X and bit 16
adds -1, and the fill helper 0x147704a90 maps those bits to wire flags
12 (Left) and 13 (Right). The diagonal table agrees: UpLeft adds
(+1, +1) and UpRight adds (-1, +1). Java's raw input uses the same
convention, so the move vector and the raw move vector now agree. An
earlier revision of this patch inverted X and contradicted the raw
move vector on every strafing frame.

diff --git a/src/main/java/net/raphimc/viabedrock/api/util/MathUtil.java b/src/main/java/net/raphimc/viabedrock/api/util/MathUtil.java
index badfaee466ea58805740e8c6ce1d8dc98139140c..f69f39244105927fd2aa4a630be77da423ac6502 100644
--- a/src/main/java/net/raphimc/viabedrock/api/util/MathUtil.java
+++ b/src/main/java/net/raphimc/viabedrock/api/util/MathUtil.java
@@ -97,8 +97,8 @@ public final class MathUtil {
 
     public static Position2f calculateMovementDirections(final Set<PlayerAuthInputData> authInputData, final boolean sneaking) {
         final float[] directions = new float[2];
-        directions[0] = authInputData.contains(PlayerAuthInputData.Left) ? 1F : authInputData.contains(PlayerAuthInputData.Right) ? -1F : 0F;
-        directions[1] = authInputData.contains(PlayerAuthInputData.Up) ? 1F : authInputData.contains(PlayerAuthInputData.Down) ? -1F : 0F;
+        directions[0] = (authInputData.contains(PlayerAuthInputData.Left) ? 1F : 0F) - (authInputData.contains(PlayerAuthInputData.Right) ? 1F : 0F);
+        directions[1] = (authInputData.contains(PlayerAuthInputData.Up) ? 1F : 0F) - (authInputData.contains(PlayerAuthInputData.Down) ? 1F : 0F);
         final boolean both = directions[0] != 0F && directions[1] != 0F;
         for (int i = 0; i < directions.length; i++) {
             if (both) {
